WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:02.135
First up,
please welcome two students

00:00:02.235 --> 00:00:04.470
at Marjory Stoneman Douglas High
in Parkland, Florida,

00:00:04.570 --> 00:00:07.006
who co-founded the
advocacy group on gun control,

00:00:07.106 --> 00:00:10.276
Never Again MSD, David Hogg
and Cameron Kasky.

00:00:10.376 --> 00:00:11.544
(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:14.447
Hey.
How you doing?

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:17.650
Pleasure.
Great to meet you.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.286
How are you, David?
All right!

00:00:23.022 --> 00:00:24.024
Wow.

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.361
How you guys doing?
You..

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:30.229
-Tired.
-Tired, yeah.

00:00:30.329 --> 00:00:33.333
You're running around
the country doing a good job.

00:00:33.433 --> 00:00:34.433
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:00:34.667 --> 00:00:35.869
Trying to make our voices heard.

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.637
Oh, you're doing that and more,
I mean,

00:00:37.737 --> 00:00:39.405
you've done a great thing in

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.674
turning your grief
into something positive.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:43.510
And you have a march?

00:00:43.610 --> 00:00:45.311
First,
let's just talk about that.

00:00:45.411 --> 00:00:48.214
I mean, the future and what's
gonna happen with this movement.

00:00:48.314 --> 00:00:50.984
It's on-- It's-- When is it?
It's scheduled for Washington?

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:52.184
It's March 24th.

00:00:52.284 --> 00:00:54.854
BILL: Okay.
A march in March on the 24th.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:56.922
And what are the goals?

00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:01.694
Well, we are...
With the march we want Americans

00:01:01.794 --> 00:01:04.864 line:0%
to stop being afraid
of demanding our politicians

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:05.965 line:0%
to take action.

00:01:06.065 --> 00:01:08.100 line:0%
They work for us,
we don't work for them.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:11.704 line:0%
-And the march is us--
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:11.804 --> 00:01:15.008
The-- The march is us coming out
and saying to our employees,

00:01:15.108 --> 00:01:16.509
"You guys suck at your job."

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:19.512
-BILL: Right. (LAUGHS)
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:19.612 --> 00:01:23.049
With-- With the march,
we want everyone to come out,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:24.617
bring their parents,
bring their kids,

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:27.920
everybody in the nation is
either a child or a former child

00:01:28.253 --> 00:01:30.656
and that's what we wanna do,
is say,

00:01:30.757 --> 00:01:32.525
"This isn't about red and blue,

00:01:32.625 --> 00:01:34.259
this is about
protecting the kids."

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:39.231
-Okay.
-(CHEERING AND APPLAUSE)

00:01:39.331 --> 00:01:42.168
And you also have a boycott,
right, in mind for--

00:01:42.268 --> 00:01:43.502
I think that's a great idea.

00:01:43.602 --> 00:01:45.505
Yeah, so what we're trying to
do with that is...

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:48.507
we essentially-- We met with
some of the legislators

00:01:48.607 --> 00:01:51.744 line:0%
in Tallahassee and we felt like
we didn't really get far enough

00:01:51.844 --> 00:01:54.847 line:0%
because they wouldn't even
discuss assault weapons there.

00:01:54.947 --> 00:01:56.382 line:0%
What they did discuss though,

00:01:56.482 --> 00:01:58.918 line:0%
was porn
as a public health emergency.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:00.520
-(CHUCKLES)
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:03.089
Which just goes to show you...
It's porn, but...

00:02:03.189 --> 00:02:05.391
-A, uh, related shooting issue.
-DAVID: Yeah.

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:09.095
-Yeah.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.563
But sadly, that's the only one

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.831
that these law-makers seemed
to care about.

00:02:12.932 --> 00:02:14.567
Right. Is that really...
(LAUGHS)

00:02:14.667 --> 00:02:15.934
That's what they said to you?

00:02:16.035 --> 00:02:17.737
They said, "Let's switch
the subject to porn"?

00:02:17.837 --> 00:02:18.670
-DAVID: Mm-hmm.
-They--

00:02:18.771 --> 00:02:19.705
BILL: And how old are you guys?

00:02:19.806 --> 00:02:20.840
-Seventeen?
-BOTH: Seventeen.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.141
BILL: Not gonna work with you.

00:02:22.241 --> 00:02:23.576
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:23.676 --> 00:02:25.711
I remember 17 and, boy,
I didn't--

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.447
Well, I say they stop looking
at that stuff

00:02:27.547 --> 00:02:29.615
and actually start looking
at our lives, you know?

00:02:29.715 --> 00:02:30.716
BILL: Right.

00:02:30.817 --> 00:02:31.817
(APPLAUSE)

00:02:31.917 --> 00:02:33.987
-So-- So--
-BILL: So-- Yeah.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:37.056
So, with the economics,
with all of that,

00:02:37.156 --> 00:02:38.824
we felt like,
at least I felt like,

00:02:38.924 --> 00:02:40.459
we weren't getting
enough movement,

00:02:40.559 --> 00:02:41.994
so I decided if the only thing

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.629
these politicians care about
is money,

00:02:43.729 --> 00:02:44.664
we'll go after their money.

00:02:44.764 --> 00:02:46.899
That's very smart.
You know, I gotta say...

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:48.000
(APPLAUSE)

00:02:48.100 --> 00:02:49.702
...watching, besides the service

00:02:49.802 --> 00:02:51.404
you're doing to the country
about guns...

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:52.905
You know, I don't have kids.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.708
And I only see what I know
about them from television,

00:02:55.808 --> 00:02:57.343
I-- I avoid them in life.

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:58.444
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:02:58.711 --> 00:03:00.213
-With good reason.
-Yeah.

00:03:00.313 --> 00:03:01.481
(BILL CHUCKLES)

00:03:01.581 --> 00:03:03.916
But watch--
I mean, you're so together.

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:05.785
And all of you, not just you,

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.288
the other people from
your school I've seen on TV:

00:03:08.388 --> 00:03:09.789
calm, articulate,

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:12.191
I honestly thought
kids were a lot stupider.

00:03:12.425 --> 00:03:14.060
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-You have really...

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:18.430
given me faith that the kids
today are actually very bright.

00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:19.532
(APPLAUSE)

00:03:19.632 --> 00:03:21.534
I-- And I'll tell you why--

00:03:21.634 --> 00:03:23.669
Way brighter than we were--

00:03:23.770 --> 00:03:26.138
It's only because they locked up
the Tide Pods.

00:03:26.238 --> 00:03:28.207
(BILL LAUGHS)

00:03:28.307 --> 00:03:30.610
In all seriousness,
I think the good thing--

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:33.212
One of the best things about
our generation, sure,

00:03:33.312 --> 00:03:35.781
people think we're lazy
and on our phones all the time

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.150
and, sure, you know,
that's me, but we don't--

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:39.285
(BILL LAUGHS)

00:03:39.385 --> 00:03:41.787
We don't respect people just
because we have to.

00:03:41.887 --> 00:03:43.322
We don't respect you
just because you have "senator"

00:03:43.422 --> 00:03:44.523
in front of your name.

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:45.958
-BILL: Right.
-And, Mr. Rubio,

00:03:46.058 --> 00:03:48.627
if you don't believe me,
watch, you know, the news.

00:03:48.727 --> 00:03:50.396
-And...
-BILL: Right.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:52.131
We don't just stand for--

00:03:52.231 --> 00:03:54.700
We don't let people
steam roll over us.

00:03:55.001 --> 00:03:58.404
We have voices and we use them,
sometimes unfortunately,

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.040
sometimes for good,
and that's why--

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.376
I think you're doing very good.
And I wanna know, how long do--

00:04:04.476 --> 00:04:07.112
Do you think you will keep
doing this,

00:04:07.613 --> 00:04:08.982
how long will this keep going?

00:04:09.082 --> 00:04:10.116
Well,
to be quite frank with you,

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:11.784
we're millennials
and we love complaining

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:13.953
more than any other generation,
so...

00:04:14.187 --> 00:04:16.022
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-CAMERON: Ask the stage manager.

00:04:16.122 --> 00:04:17.789
Could you--
(LAUGHS)

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.458
Why, were you bitching about
something here?

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:20.993
No, uh, look,

00:04:21.093 --> 00:04:23.562
a lot of people are trying to
take us down quickly,

00:04:23.662 --> 00:04:25.564
they're trying to discredit us,
they're trying to say

00:04:25.664 --> 00:04:27.400
we don't know
what we're talking about.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.401
Well, until you've been on
the receiving end--

00:04:29.501 --> 00:04:30.736 line:0%
BILL: Some of them even called
you actors.

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.004 line:0%
Well, I am an actor, actually.

00:04:32.105 --> 00:04:33.505 line:0%
-BILL: Oh.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:33.605 --> 00:04:35.240 line:0%
I'm in<i> Spring Awakening</i>
right now

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:36.542 line:0%
at the
Barclay Performing Arts Center,

00:04:36.642 --> 00:04:38.610 line:0%
-it's a great show.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:38.711 --> 00:04:41.281
What I'm saying is,
you can say we don't know

00:04:41.381 --> 00:04:43.549
what we're talking about
because we're 17 years old,

00:04:43.649 --> 00:04:46.718
but until you've been on
the receiving end of an AR-15,

00:04:46.818 --> 00:04:48.354
until you've been locked into
your cl--

00:04:48.454 --> 00:04:50.823
Look, Wayne LaPierre,
Dana Loesch... (SHUDDERS)

00:04:50.923 --> 00:04:52.158
-BILL: Right.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:04:52.258 --> 00:04:54.126
I don't know--
I don't know if you guys

00:04:54.226 --> 00:04:55.227
have ever had to
deal with that,

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:57.029
but as far as I know,
that's not the case.

00:04:57.129 --> 00:04:58.531
We've been locked in
a classroom,

00:04:58.631 --> 00:05:01.333
we have seen our friends text
their parents goodbye,

00:05:01.734 --> 00:05:03.269
we are the experts,

00:05:03.502 --> 00:05:05.371
we know exactly
what we're talking about,

00:05:05.471 --> 00:05:08.440
how dare you tell us
we don't know what we're--

00:05:08.540 --> 00:05:09.775
BILL: I'm friend. Friend!

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:10.976
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:05:11.076 --> 00:05:13.980
Let's, uh, take that again.
(CLAPS)

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:18.784
Cameron, scene two.
Uh... Yes, agreed.

00:05:19.018 --> 00:05:22.588
What I'm asking is, like,
in six months, say,

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.890
if you haven't gotten
the change you wanted,

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:26.758
you're gonna graduate high
school at some point, right?

00:05:26.859 --> 00:05:27.860
Hopefully.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:29.328
(LAUGHS)
I might not. Um...

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.429
(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:05:30.529 --> 00:05:31.730
BILL: Would you see doing this
as a career?

00:05:31.830 --> 00:05:32.732
Blowing off college.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:35.101
Because, honestly, guys,
college is a bunch of bullshit.

00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:36.202
(AUDIENCE GROANS)

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.838
Kidding, kids, kidding,
it's great. Yeah, college.

00:05:38.938 --> 00:05:39.838
Uh...

00:05:40.239 --> 00:05:42.108
You probably, you know,
would learn more

00:05:42.208 --> 00:05:43.910
or just as much, you know,
I mean,

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:45.444
you already have
this great platform.

00:05:45.544 --> 00:05:47.913
We'd certainly learn more than
our politicians are--

00:05:48.013 --> 00:05:49.248
What they take action on.

00:05:49.348 --> 00:05:51.817
BILL: Right. Well, I do think
you're gonna get something done,

00:05:51.917 --> 00:05:52.918
I really do.

00:05:53.018 --> 00:05:55.154
I mean, we have never quite seen
change like this,

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.855
or at least people
receptive to it.

00:05:56.955 --> 00:05:58.557
And I think part of the reason
for that is:

00:05:58.657 --> 00:06:00.960
we've kept reminding people
that this isn't about us,

00:06:01.060 --> 00:06:02.962
this isn't about Democrats
or Republicans,

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.664 line:0%
this is about Americans
and those 17 individuals

00:06:05.765 --> 00:06:07.065 line:0%
that lost their lives that day,

00:06:07.165 --> 00:06:08.534 line:0%
that's what this
should really be about.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:10.770 line:0%
CAMERON: We're not targeting
people's guns.

00:06:10.870 --> 00:06:14.740
My father's a police officer,
his father's former FBI,

00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:17.543
we have guns in our houses,
we're not trying to tear apart

00:06:17.643 --> 00:06:21.079
the Second Amendment,
we are just kids begging for

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.415
our lives getting murdered
in our classrooms.

00:06:23.515 --> 00:06:24.984
But, honestly, I think that's

00:06:25.084 --> 00:06:26.252
part of the problem
in this country,

00:06:26.352 --> 00:06:28.354
is that nobody goes after
the Second Amendment.

00:06:28.955 --> 00:06:30.456
Nothing is really gonna change

00:06:30.556 --> 00:06:32.224
unless somebody
talks about that.

00:06:32.324 --> 00:06:34.961
The reason why this country
is different is 'cause we

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:36.161
treat guns as a right,

00:06:36.261 --> 00:06:38.464
other countries
treat it as a privilege.

00:06:38.764 --> 00:06:40.732
And every debate begins,
with even--

00:06:40.833 --> 00:06:44.904
(APPLAUSE)

00:06:45.004 --> 00:06:48.006
Even the liberal side, uh,
you know,

00:06:48.106 --> 00:06:50.042
just bowing down to the
Second Amendment

00:06:50.142 --> 00:06:52.711
and I don't know if that's
the right approach.

00:06:52.811 --> 00:06:56.315
The Second Amendment is a very,
very good piece

00:06:56.415 --> 00:06:58.484
of rhetoric defense
that I've seen a lot,

00:06:58.584 --> 00:07:03.288
because they put it as if
we're attacking a right

00:07:03.388 --> 00:07:05.657
that you're born with,
and at the end of the day,

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.126
a 19-year-old--

00:07:07.226 --> 00:07:08.561
BILL: But it is if you're
an American.

00:07:08.661 --> 00:07:09.528
If you're an American.

00:07:09.829 --> 00:07:11.864
A 19-year-old bought
a weapon that you don't need

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:13.766
to keep robbers and bears
out of your house.

00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:18.170
And if that kid had seen
a professional for five minutes

00:07:18.404 --> 00:07:19.871
they wouldn't have said,
"You need a gun,"

00:07:19.972 --> 00:07:21.274
they would have said,
"You need a councillor."

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:23.175
And that was just
allowed to happen.

00:07:23.742 --> 00:07:26.879
-BILL: Okay.
-(APPLAUSE)

00:07:26.979 --> 00:07:30.349
So, one of your classmates,
I think her name was Samantha...

00:07:31.317 --> 00:07:33.819
and Trump called her and the
first thing he said to her was,

00:07:33.919 --> 00:07:36.989
"I heard you're a big fan."
(LAUGHS)

00:07:37.089 --> 00:07:38.690
That sounds about right.
I didn't even know about that,

00:07:38.790 --> 00:07:39.926
-but that sounds about right.
-BILL: Oh, really?

00:07:40.026 --> 00:07:41.060
Do you know
who I'm talking about?

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:42.394
-I think so.
-BILL: Yeah.

00:07:42.494 --> 00:07:43.562
And she said,

00:07:43.662 --> 00:07:45.964
"I was never so unimpressed
with someone in my life."

00:07:46.065 --> 00:07:47.066
(APPLAUSE)

00:07:47.399 --> 00:07:48.700
Yeah, I actually hung up on
the White House the other day.

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:49.968
BILL:
You hung up on the White House?

00:07:50.068 --> 00:07:51.737
Yeah, because they called us
the day before--

00:07:51.837 --> 00:07:52.805
BILL: Surprised you got through.

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.374
-Well, no, they called me.
-BILL: Oh.

00:07:55.474 --> 00:07:58.211
They actually called me the day
before the listening session

00:07:58.311 --> 00:07:59.945
and asked if
we were going to come.

00:08:00.045 --> 00:08:00.912
And I said,

00:08:01.213 --> 00:08:02.714
"I'm not coming because we
expect President Trump

00:08:02.814 --> 00:08:04.216
to come to the CNN town hall,"

00:08:04.317 --> 00:08:06.452
which he never declined
an invitation from,

00:08:06.552 --> 00:08:08.954
and the fact that they called us
the day before,

00:08:09.054 --> 00:08:10.422
I found very offensive,

00:08:10.522 --> 00:08:12.391
considering the fact that there
are funerals the next day,

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:14.292
there's mourning
we still had to do.

00:08:14.393 --> 00:08:16.695
And I ended on this message with
them, I said,

00:08:16.795 --> 00:08:19.265
"President Trump-- We don't need
to listen to President Trump,

00:08:19.365 --> 00:08:21.834
President Trump needs to listen
to the screams of the children

00:08:21.934 --> 00:08:23.235
and the screams of this nation."

00:08:23.336 --> 00:08:25.103
(APPLAUSE)

00:08:25.203 --> 00:08:26.272
Well, listen,

00:08:26.372 --> 00:08:28.607
I want you to know something
about President Trump

00:08:28.708 --> 00:08:30.843
because you haven't been around
long enough

00:08:30.943 --> 00:08:32.311
to see a lot of presidents,

00:08:32.411 --> 00:08:34.346
who's the first one
you remember, Bush?

00:08:34.446 --> 00:08:37.316
I was at my first Obama rally
when I was seven-years-old.

00:08:37.416 --> 00:08:40.219
Seven-years-old, so you don't
even remember Bush hardly!

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:42.354
I remember hearing
a lot about Bush.

00:08:42.454 --> 00:08:44.590
-BILL: Yeah.
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:08:45.291 --> 00:08:47.393
I'm sure all good.
Anyway, uh...

00:08:47.760 --> 00:08:51.897
But Bush, Obama, Clinton,
they all go in one basket,

00:08:51.997 --> 00:08:54.766
I, you know, happen to fall
with the Democrats usually,

00:08:54.867 --> 00:08:56.435
-but... (LAUGHS)
-DAVID: Shock.

00:08:56.535 --> 00:08:59.004
Surprising.
But they're all in one kettle,

00:08:59.104 --> 00:09:01.974
and then there's this...
thing that happened,

00:09:02.074 --> 00:09:05.544
-this virus from outer space...
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)

00:09:05.644 --> 00:09:06.645
...that took over.

00:09:07.012 --> 00:09:10.182
I just want you to know how much
this is not like anything that's

00:09:10.282 --> 00:09:12.585
ever, ever,
ever happened before,

00:09:12.685 --> 00:09:16.021
and hopefully will not be
in your future.

00:09:16.121 --> 00:09:19.591
And I mean this sincerely,
I really do,

00:09:19.825 --> 00:09:21.927
to all of the generations
before us,

00:09:22.127 --> 00:09:24.130
we sincerely accept
your apology.

00:09:24.230 --> 00:09:27.399
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS)
-And we appreciate that you are

00:09:27.499 --> 00:09:30.068
